# Local-only sidecars carrying personal context, release-timeline details,
# parallel-project references, and machine-specific paths. The public tracked
# CLAUDE.md / docs/context.md are sanitised versions; the .local.md files stay
# on the author's machine.
CLAUDE.local.md
docs/context.local.md
docs/planning/private/

# HuggingFace Hub upload staging area. Contains LoRA .safetensors + draft model
# cards before they are pushed to HF Hub. Not part of the public repo.
models/hf-staging/

# Playwright MCP runtime scratch (browser snapshots, console logs). Agent
# runtime artifact, not source. Not part of the public repo.
.playwright-mcp/

# Training-artifact captures (validation grids, manifests) from in-flight LoRA
# training. Ships publicly alongside the relevant LoRA release on HuggingFace
# Hub, not in this repo.
train-artifacts/

# Pitch materials, sketches, and ad-hoc spot-check outputs from the maintainer's
# private workflow. Not part of the public artifact.
pitch-materials/
local-spot-check/
soutine-after-*.png
soutine-before-*.png

# Bulk dataset content. The dataset-mosaic protocol's worked-example Python
# scripts under datasets/<name>/*.py ship publicly; image bytes, training ZIPs,
# manifests, gallery state, generated HTML, and rejected-image piles do not.
datasets/**/raw/
datasets/**/raw_orig/
datasets/**/rejected/
datasets/**/processed/
datasets/**/validation/
datasets/**/_civitai_staging/
datasets/**/gallery-state*
datasets/**/captions/
datasets/**/*.zip
datasets/**/*.csv
datasets/**/*.jpg
datasets/**/*.jpeg
datasets/**/*.png
datasets/**/*.json
datasets/**/*.html
datasets/**/*.txt

# --- agent-ops-harness ---
# The bundle at tools/agent-ops-harness/ and the runtime config ARE tracked: they are
# generic, MIT, and part of how this repo is worked on. What stays local:
#
# The priorities / ops-state files live under docs/planning/private/ (already ignored
# above). They carry release timing and work-in-progress state that the public
# workshop-facing repo should not ship.
#
# The ship-gate session hooks are wired in .claude/settings.local.json so they fire on
# the maintainer's machine only. A student cloning this repo gets no trunk-divergence
# banner and no hook they did not ask for.
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- workshop deck working material (2026-08-07) ---
# The deck lives in Canva; what lands on disk here is working scrap. deck-assets/
# additionally mixes workshop media with a personal portrait and stills from a
# separate project, so none of it ships from this public repo.
canva-*.png
canva-*.yml
slow-interpolation-workshop.pptx
renoir-dataset-mosaic.png
workshop-qr.png
deck-assets/

# --- generated ---
# Built by tools/gallery.py from whatever is in outputs/. Regenerate, never commit.
gallery.html

# Review notes the maintainer types into the render gallery and exports back to
# the repo root. Unreleased-work commentary, and on occasion a client or venue
# name. This repo is public. See docs/manual/render-gallery.md.
gallery-feedback.json

# Maintainer-local MCP servers (Canva, for the deck). Not part of the pipeline;
# a student cloning this repo should not be offered a Canva server.
.mcp.json

# Glance export: build artifact, regenerate with tools/glance_export.py
outputs/_glance/
outputs/_glance-renders/
outputs/_glance-deploy/

# --- media archive kit ---
tools/.env
tools/data/kb-export/
tools/data/media-vectors/
tools/media-engine/cache/
tools/media-engine/runs/
tools/media-engine/dist/
outputs/

# Glance dataset-mosaic sites: viewer payload + thumbnails derived from raw/ (image bytes stay out; rebuild with tools/mosaic-glance/build_mosaic_archive.py)
tools/mosaic-glance/site*/

# --- private working surface (2026-08-19) -------------------------------
# This repo is the PUBLIC workshop package. The rules above already keep the
# bulk out, but 218 files were still untracked-and-unignored, which is one
# `git add -A` from being published. Everything below is either a run
# artifact, a deployment identifier, or a screenshot: none of it is source,
# and none of it is workshop material.
#
# 218 measured against the upstream tree. The commit that added this block
# said 445, which was wrong: `git status` was reporting against a LOCAL HEAD
# that was behind origin/main, so ~227 files already committed upstream
# looked untracked. Corrected here; see the follow-up commit. The rules
# themselves were unaffected, because every hazard they name was verified
# individually as genuinely absent from the upstream tree.
#
# Deliberately NOT covered here, because they need a decision rather than a
# rule: examples/configs/** (generic technique configs are workshop material,
# but nyc-billboard/, course-of-empire/ and arendt/ look like commissions),
# and tools/agent-ops-harness/ (the note above says the bundle IS meant to be
# tracked, so its being untracked is an oversight, not a policy).

# Media-archive ingest run logs. One file per run, machine-generated, 160 of
# them. Regenerate by running an ingest; never commit.
knowledge/operations/media-ingest/

# Supabase CLI local state. The stock `supabase/.gitignore` was never adopted
# here, so `.temp/linked-project.json` sat untracked and unignored in a public
# repo carrying the project ref AND the organization id. Not a credential, but
# it names infrastructure that is not part of the workshop package, and it is
# machine-generated by `supabase link` rather than authored.
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/

# Vercel project pins for private deployments. Not credentials, but they name
# and target deployments that are not part of the workshop package.
# Two patterns, not one: the main field's pin is `.glance-vercel.json` with
# nothing between the prefix and the suffix, so a single glob misses it.
.glance-vercel.json
.glance-*-vercel.json

# A live tunnel address, and the render gallery's exported review state.
tunnel-url.txt
review-gate.json

# Loose screenshots at the repo root. The Glance/gallery workflow is
# screenshot-driven, so these accumulate, and a screenshot of a signed-in
# session renders a credential as readable text. One in this pile is a cloud
# billing page. The equivalent rule was added upstream only AFTER a live key
# was found sitting in four browser dumps; added here before that happens.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
